1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,791
Seven lessons. Eight objectives. One web server. Today you prove you can do all of it.

2
00:00:06,341 --> 00:00:08,525
A half-built web tier is waiting.

3
00:00:08,525 --> 00:00:09,452
A static site,

4
00:00:09,452 --> 00:00:10,511
a reverse proxy,

5
00:00:10,511 --> 00:00:11,769
secure web traffic,

6
00:00:11,769 --> 00:00:13,027
two apps behind it,

7
00:00:13,027 --> 00:00:13,490
limits,

8
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:14,682
and a slow report.

9
00:00:15,232 --> 00:00:17,223
Nobody tells you what is wrong.

10
00:00:17,223 --> 00:00:17,993
You find it,

11
00:00:17,993 --> 00:00:18,443
fix it,

12
00:00:18,443 --> 00:00:19,214
document it,

13
00:00:19,214 --> 00:00:21,461
and a judge checks every objective.

14
00:00:22,011 --> 00:00:23,291
Prove the whole domain.

15
00:00:24,841 --> 00:00:27,913
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

16
00:00:28,463 --> 00:00:32,772
One: the whole domain on one page, so you see how the seven lessons connect.

17
00:00:33,322 --> 00:00:34,584
Two: a live demo.

18
00:00:34,584 --> 00:00:35,921
One real engine X,

19
00:00:35,921 --> 00:00:37,183
eight objectives,

20
00:00:37,183 --> 00:00:40,746
from a static page all the way to a slow report.

21
00:00:41,296 --> 00:00:45,456
Three: for each one, we find the evidence first, then fix it, then prove it.

22
00:00:46,006 --> 00:00:47,389
Four: we write our notes,

23
00:00:47,389 --> 00:00:48,107
and clean up.

24
00:00:48,107 --> 00:00:48,937
Then your turn,

25
00:00:48,937 --> 00:00:51,425
with a lab that judges you with eight checks.

26
00:00:51,975 --> 00:00:55,076
This is the mastery lesson of the web servers domain.

27
00:00:55,076 --> 00:00:56,538
If you can do this alone,

28
00:00:56,538 --> 00:00:57,650
you own the domain.

29
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:59,480
Prove the whole domain.

30
00:01:01,530 --> 00:01:03,215
The whole domain on one page.

31
00:01:03,765 --> 00:01:07,195
Objective one and two: engine X serves static files,

32
00:01:07,195 --> 00:01:08,317
tests its config,

33
00:01:08,317 --> 00:01:10,229
and reloads without stopping.

34
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:14,470
Objective three: the reverse proxy sends traffic to an app,

35
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:17,222
and passes the real host and client address.

36
00:01:17,772 --> 00:01:22,423
Objective four: H T T P S with a certificate that matches the name.

37
00:01:22,973 --> 00:01:25,959
Objective five: a pool of apps, with a health check.

38
00:01:26,509 --> 00:01:30,456
Objective six: the logs and the status codes tell you what happened.

39
00:01:31,006 --> 00:01:36,745
Objective seven: limits and secure defaults. Objective eight: troubleshoot when it breaks.

40
00:01:38,295 --> 00:01:43,500
Go to the lab folder.

41
00:01:45,050 --> 00:01:46,949
Look around. Type: L S.

42
00:01:47,499 --> 00:01:48,255
The config,

43
00:01:48,255 --> 00:01:49,218
a certificate,

44
00:01:49,218 --> 00:01:50,181
a site folder,

45
00:01:50,181 --> 00:01:51,625
a log of old traffic.

46
00:01:51,625 --> 00:01:52,725
Behind engine X,

47
00:01:52,725 --> 00:01:54,582
two small apps are running.

48
00:01:55,132 --> 00:01:59,996
Run the judge, show the last line.

49
00:02:00,546 --> 00:02:03,042
Zero out of eight. That is our starting line.

50
00:02:03,592 --> 00:02:08,328
First, a tiny helper that prints only the status code. We will use it all the way.

51
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:26,072
Type the helper.

52
00:02:26,622 --> 00:02:34,153
Objective one: ask for the site.

53
00:02:34,703 --> 00:02:38,372
Four oh four. The site is there, but engine X cannot find it.

54
00:02:38,922 --> 00:02:43,999
Find the root.

55
00:02:44,550 --> 00:02:49,947
Line nineteen says site, with two E's. A typo. The real folder is site, with one.

56
00:02:50,497 --> 00:02:54,252
Open the config in vim.

57
00:02:54,802 --> 00:02:58,023
Go to line nineteen, and fix the root path. Then save.

58
00:03:06,573 --> 00:03:13,933
Test, then reload.

59
00:03:14,483 --> 00:03:17,320
Test first, then reload, without stopping anything.

60
00:03:17,870 --> 00:03:22,500
Ask again.

61
00:03:23,050 --> 00:03:25,140
Two hundred. The static site works.

62
00:03:25,690 --> 00:03:35,930
Objective three: what does the app see?

63
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:37,449
The app answers,

64
00:03:37,449 --> 00:03:39,326
but it thinks the host is pool,

65
00:03:39,326 --> 00:03:42,110
and it sees no client address and no protocol.

66
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:43,563
We have to pass them on.

67
00:03:44,113 --> 00:03:47,868
Open the config again.

68
00:03:48,418 --> 00:03:49,333
On line twenty,

69
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:53,240
replace the location with one that sets three headers: the host,

70
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:54,705
the real client address,

71
00:03:54,705 --> 00:03:56,354
and the forwarded protocol.

72
00:04:21,204 --> 00:04:27,305
Test, then reload.

73
00:04:27,855 --> 00:04:35,471
Ask the app again.

74
00:04:36,021 --> 00:04:39,882
Now the app sees the real host, the client address, and the protocol.

75
00:04:40,432 --> 00:04:52,187
Objective four: whose name is on the certificate?

76
00:04:52,737 --> 00:04:57,238
Wrong dot example. The site is local host, so clients would refuse it.

77
00:04:57,788 --> 00:05:28,673
Make a new certificate.

78
00:05:29,223 --> 00:05:31,911
Reload.

79
00:05:32,461 --> 00:05:43,384
Check the secure site.

80
00:05:43,934 --> 00:05:46,835
Two hundred, and this time the certificate verifies.

81
00:05:47,385 --> 00:06:02,660
Objective five: ask the pool four times.

82
00:06:03,210 --> 00:06:08,692
Four times app A. App B never answers. A wrong port is hiding in the upstream block.

83
00:06:09,242 --> 00:06:12,997
Open the config.

84
00:06:13,547 --> 00:06:14,642
On line fifteen,

85
00:06:14,642 --> 00:06:17,241
fix the port to eighty-two fifty-five.

86
00:06:17,241 --> 00:06:18,883
Then after the location,

87
00:06:18,883 --> 00:06:21,483
add a health endpoint that answers ok.

88
00:06:34,533 --> 00:06:40,634
Test, then reload.

89
00:06:41,184 --> 00:06:54,432
Ask the pool four times.

90
00:06:54,982 --> 00:06:58,246
A, B, A, B. Round robin, with both apps in the pool.

91
00:06:58,796 --> 00:07:04,706
Check the health endpoint.

92
00:07:05,256 --> 00:07:09,522
Two hundred. A load balancer can now ask engine X if it is alive.

93
00:07:10,072 --> 00:07:25,112
Objective six: count the failures.

94
00:07:25,662 --> 00:07:28,030
Seven failures in a day of old traffic.

95
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:46,628
Which failure was the most common?

96
00:07:47,178 --> 00:07:51,850
Three times five oh two. The app was refusing connections more than anything else.

97
00:07:52,400 --> 00:08:00,912
Write the two answers.

98
00:08:01,462 --> 00:08:04,342
Read it back. Type: cat, answers dot text.

99
00:08:04,892 --> 00:08:13,191
Objective seven: send a big upload.

100
00:08:13,741 --> 00:08:23,128
Upload it.

101
00:08:23,678 --> 00:08:28,776
Two hundred. The server accepts two megabytes, when the limit is a hundred. Too generous.

102
00:08:29,326 --> 00:08:38,649
What does the server header say?

103
00:08:39,199 --> 00:08:42,591
It tells everyone the exact version. Attackers love that.

104
00:08:43,141 --> 00:08:46,896
Open the config.

105
00:08:47,446 --> 00:08:48,387
On line twelve,

106
00:08:48,387 --> 00:08:50,271
set the limit to one megabyte,

107
00:08:50,271 --> 00:08:51,904
and add server tokens off,

108
00:08:51,904 --> 00:08:52,971
on the next line.

109
00:09:01,621 --> 00:09:07,722
Test, then reload.

110
00:09:08,272 --> 00:09:18,107
Upload again.

111
00:09:18,657 --> 00:09:22,881
Four thirteen. Request too large. Refused before it reaches the app.

112
00:09:23,431 --> 00:09:31,943
Server header again.

113
00:09:32,493 --> 00:09:34,562
Just engine X. No version.

114
00:09:35,112 --> 00:09:42,280
Objective eight: the slow report.

115
00:09:42,830 --> 00:09:47,268
Five oh four. Gateway timeout. Evidence first: ask the error log.

116
00:09:47,818 --> 00:09:57,311
Ask the error log.

117
00:09:57,861 --> 00:10:02,021
Up stream timed out. The app is alive, but engine X stopped waiting.

118
00:10:02,571 --> 00:10:06,326
Open the config.

119
00:10:06,876 --> 00:10:11,740
The report takes three seconds, and the timeout is one. On line thirty, make it ten.

120
00:10:16,990 --> 00:10:23,091
Test, then reload.

121
00:10:23,641 --> 00:10:29,508
Ask for the report.

122
00:10:30,058 --> 00:10:33,983
Two hundred, after three seconds. The slow report finally comes.

123
00:10:34,533 --> 00:10:44,218
Document your results.

124
00:10:44,768 --> 00:10:47,542
Read it back. Type: cat, notes dot text.

125
00:10:48,092 --> 00:10:51,825
Results, troubleshooting, cleanup. Three lines your team can read.

126
00:10:52,375 --> 00:10:54,828
Run the judge.

127
00:10:55,378 --> 00:10:58,749
Eight checks, one for each part of the domain. Eight out of eight.

128
00:10:59,299 --> 00:11:01,262
Clean up.

129
00:11:01,812 --> 00:11:04,286
Engine X, both apps, everything removed.

130
00:11:04,836 --> 00:11:14,415
Are the ports free? Count the lines.

131
00:11:14,965 --> 00:11:17,973
Zero. Nothing listens, nothing is left behind.

132
00:11:19,523 --> 00:11:24,664
Your task. A half-built web tier, and eight things to prove. Find the evidence, then fix.

133
00:11:25,214 --> 00:11:28,272
One: the static site and the config test.

134
00:11:28,272 --> 00:11:29,986
